# Install a flat node_modules instead of pnpm's isolated store.
#
# Two reasons, both about React Native. Metro cannot follow pnpm's isolated
# layout reliably — a package's own dependencies live in a sibling directory
# under .pnpm and resolution depends on walking up from the importing file,
# which breaks differently on different filesystems. And this repo lives on a
# FUSE mount that cannot create symlinks, so pnpm already falls back to copying
# here: the local tree was effectively hoisted while EAS, on ext4, installed
# isolated. That divergence is invisible until a CI build fails to resolve a
# transitive dependency the local build found by luck.
#
# Hoisting costs pnpm's protection against phantom dependencies. Making local
# and CI produce the same tree is worth more.
node-linker=hoisted
